  "notes": "Xiaomi MiTV-MSSP1 (codename nino), Android TV 9 (SDK 28), firmware PI.5925 release-keys.\n\nApply: TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/xiaomi-mitv-mssp1/debloat.txt\nUndo:  TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/xiaomi-mitv-mssp1/debloat.txt\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nStock launcher: com.google.android.tvlauncher. It is not listed here;\nlauncher/build-and-install.sh handles its cutover after the replacement Home is installed.\nLive TV: com.mediatek.wwtv.tvcenter; HDMI/tuner service: com.mediatek.tvinput. Both kept enabled.\nAlso kept enabled: com.xiaomi.mitv.updateservice (firmware updates), Google Assistant,\nChromecast, com.xiaomi.mitv.mediaexplorer (USB media), Play Store and Play Services.\n\nChecks on this set: the replacement Home survived reboot; the owner confirmed streaming-app\nplayback. All eight packages below remain disabled.\nNo package from this list had to be re-enabled during those checks.\nThis is nino / PI.5925, not the MSSP0 (amelie), MSSP2 (volver) or MSSP3 (machuca) firmware.\nXiaomi telemetry",
